<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!-- homr 0.7.0, unmodified, reading a printed 4/4 piano page rendered at 300 dpi in grey as the scan server renders it
     (issue #495 BUG-03). Each bar: an eighth rest or an eighth, three eighths, a grace note and four eighths over two
     half-note chords. Eight of the page's bars, cut out as homr wrote them. homr wrote 5/4: it never reads the upper
     number, it writes the median length of its own bars. Bars 3-5 and 8: the left hand written after the right hand's
     first note instead of with it (six quarters). Bar 6: one note of the left hand's first chord put on the upper staff
     (six quarters). Bar 7: the left hand an eighth late throughout (four and a half quarters). -->
